# The build context is `.`, so without this the daemon receives `.venv` -- hundreds of megabytes of
# platform-specific wheels that the image then reinstalls anyway, and which would invalidate the
# layer cache on every local `pip install`.
#
# Mirrors `.gitignore` for the caches, and adds the things that are tracked but have no business in
# an image: the audit bundle is evidence about a run on somebody's laptop, and the tests are not
# installed by `pip install -e .`.

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

.git/
.github/

# Tracked, and deliberately not in the image.
audit/
tests/
docs/
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md

# Secrets never enter a build context. `.env.example` is committed and is not one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
